### **AISTF ACTION: Architecting Core Data Schemas**

**Objective:** To define the TypeScript interfaces for LegendaryAchievement and LegacyTalent and integrate them into the
CognitiveCoreState.

**File to be Modified:** src/lib/stores/useCognitiveCore.ts

**Proposed Code Additions:**

TypeScript

// src/lib/stores/useCognitiveCore.ts

// ... (existing imports)

// \--- NEW DATA STRUCTURES \---

/\*\* \* @interface LegendaryAchievement \* @description Represents a single, high-impact achievement that awards Prestige Points. \* This is the raw data model for an achievement.
\*/
export interface LegendaryAchievement {
id: string; // Unique identifier (e.g., 'DEFEAT_SHADOW_KING')
name: string; // Player-facing name (e.g., 'Throne Breaker')
description: string; // Details of the achievement
ppValue: number; // The amount of Prestige Points awarded
}

/\*\* \* @interface LegacyTalent \* @description Represents a permanent, account-wide bonus unlocked via a Prestige Reset. \* This is the raw data model for a talent.
\*/
export interface LegacyTalent {
id: string; // Unique identifier (e.g., 'LEGACY_OF_THE_PIONEER')
name: string; // Player-facing name (e.g., 'Legacy of the Pioneer')
description: string; // What the talent does
cost: number; // The PP cost to unlock this talent during a "Rebirth"
}

/\*\* \* @interface PlayerAchievementState \* @description Tracks the completion state of a Legendary Achievement for a player.
\*/
export interface PlayerAchievementState {
achievementId: string;
isCompleted: boolean;
completedTimestamp?: number;
}

// \--- UPDATE TO THE ZUSTAND STORE \---

export interface CognitiveCoreState {
// ... (existing properties like prestigeLevel, characterLevel, etc.)

// \--- PRESTIGE SYSTEM STATE \---

/\*\* \* @property {LegendaryAchievement\[\]} legendaryAchievements \* @description A read-only list of all possible Legendary Achievements in the game. \* This would be loaded from a static game data file.
\*/
legendaryAchievements: LegendaryAchievement\[\];

/\*\* \* @property {LegacyTalent\[\]} legacyTalents \* @description A read-only list of all possible Legacy Talents. \* This would also be loaded from static game data.
\*/
legacyTalents: LegacyTalent\[\];

/\*\* \* @property {PlayerAchievementState\[\]} playerAchievements \* @description Tracks the completion status of achievements for the current player. \* This is the dynamic data that would be saved and loaded per player account.
\*/
playerAchievements: PlayerAchievementState\[\];

/\*\* \* @property {string\[\]} unlockedLegacyTalents \* @description A list of LegacyTalent IDs that the player has unlocked.
\*/
unlockedLegacyTalents: string\[\];
}

// ... (rest of the store implementation)

**Reasoning & Justification:**

- **Separation of Concerns:** By defining LegendaryAchievement and LegacyTalent as static, read-only data, we separate
  the _game's design_ from the _player's state_. The PlayerAchievementState and unlockedLegacyTalents arrays are the
  dynamic data that will change as the user plays. This is a robust and scalable approach.
- **Type Safety:** Using TypeScript interfaces ensures that we cannot accidentally introduce malformed achievement or
  talent data into our application state, preventing a common source of bugs.
- **Clarity & Readability:** This structure makes the purpose of each data point explicit. It is immediately clear what
  data is static game configuration versus what is dynamic player progression.

This code provides the necessary schema for the engineering team to proceed with the next task: building the economic
simulation script that will use these structures.

---

Acknowledged. The data schemas are now architected and integrated into the CognitiveCoreState. This provides the
structural foundation for the Prestige System.

